-- L4DEL: intuition: As the kernel of the Hilbert transform is well approximated by `dirichletApprox`, up to an error controlled by `12 * niceKernel r`, we may bound `czOperator K` in terms of these. As the approximation only works in the interval `[-π, π]`, this statement is only true for a point `x` in `[2, 3]` and a function supported in `[1, 4]`, as this means all values of the approximation that will show up will be in `[-2, 2] ⊆ [-π, π]`.

