@file Carleson/ToMathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/NoAtoms/Defs.lean
@decl MeasureTheory.NoAtoms'
-- L4DEL: title: Measure `μ` *has no atoms* if for any measurable set `s` with positive `μ`-measure, there exists a measurable `t ⊆ s` such that `0 < μ t < μ s`
-- L4DEL: intuition: Measure `μ` *has no atoms* if for any measurable set `s` with positive `μ`-measure, there exists a measurable `t ⊆ s` such that `0 < μ t < μ s`. While this implies `μ {x} = 0`, the converse is not true.

